{=============================================================================
  1 GW power plant cooled by river water (exercise 6.22)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0236
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Teaching exercise (ULiège, thermodynamique appliquée, THD09, R04,
  exercise 6.22). A plant of 1 GW rejects heat to river water. The
  condensation pressure fixes the saturation temperature, taken as the
  low temperature of an equivalent Carnot cycle. The file returns the
  Carnot efficiency, the condenser heat rate and the river temperature
  rise after perfect mixing.

  eta = (t_c - t_f)/(t_c + 273.15) uses both temperatures in °C.
  This is not a cycle of states, so there are no diagram-state arrays.

  Inputs : t_c, P_cond, W_dot, q_v_w, rho_w, c_p_w
  Outputs: eta, Q_dot_cond, DELTAt_w
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : Stéphane Bertagnolio, ULiège THD09 - see README.md
  Licence: MIT. Status: verified against the EES stored solution.
=============================================================================}

"!Exercise 6.22"
"THD09 - R04 - Ex04. Exercise 6.22, as in the original."

"!Data"
t_c=550 [C]                                              "t_c of the equivalent Carnot cycle [C]"
P_cond=10000 [Pa]                                        "condensation pressure [Pa]"
W_dot=1000E6 [W]                                         "power [W]"

"!Condensation temperature"
"The condensation pressure gives the condensation temperature (saturated state), and thus the low temperature of the equivalent Carnot cycle, as in the original."
t_cond=temperature(Water,P=P_cond,x=1)                  "saturation temperature of Water at P_cond and x = 1 [C]"
t_f=t_cond                                               "low temperature of the equivalent Carnot cycle [C]"

"!Carnot efficiency of the engine cycle"
eta=(t_c-t_f)/(t_c+273.15)                               "Carnot efficiency between t_c and t_f, both in C [-]"

"!Condenser power"
eta=W_dot/Q_dot_utile                                    "efficiency written as W_dot/Q_dot_utile, as in the original [-]"
Q_dot_cond=Q_dot_utile-W_dot                             "condenser heat rate [W]"

"!River water flow"
q_v_w=8*60*10/60                                         "river volume flow, as written [m^3/s]"
q_m_w=q_v_w*rho_w                                        "river mass flow [kg/s]"
rho_w=1000 [kg/m^3]                                      "river water density [kg/m^3]"

"!River temperature rise"
"Assuming perfect mixing in the river after the heat is rejected, as in the original."
Q_dot_cond=q_m_w*c_p_w*DELTAt_w                          "energy balance on the river water [W]"
c_p_w=4187                                               "specific heat of river water [J/kg-K]"
